ion "The expression ${0}^{100}$ means $0$ multiplied by itself $100$ times. So, since $0$ times any number is $0$,  we have ${0}^{100}=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e6aa17b9-5d07-5942-b17f-d9ecdeadf17f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e6aa17b9-5d07-5942-b17f-d9ecdeadf17f" :answer-field/id #uuid "e6aa17b9-5d07-5942-b17f-d9ecdeadf17f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2302e26d-bd2a-5b1a-8f7a-69798b8f6993" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2302e26d-bd2a-5b1a-8f7a-69798b8f6993" "answer-1a7dce17-7be1-56eb-a50a-a76695d8a7f9" "answer-5341034a-5c70-550f-94f0-6292fdc42b66" "answer-a7772d20-a081-52a3-96c2-6ccd8c426e27" "answer-c6a11e57-9c69-5b62-be44-f709d7198d5a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2302e26d-bd2a-5b1a-8f7a-69798b8f6993" :answer/id #uuid "2302e26d-bd2a-5b1a-8f7a-69798b8f6993" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1a7dce17-7be1-56eb-a50a-a76695d8a7f9" :answer/id #uuid "1a7dce17-7be1-56eb-a50a-a76695d8a7f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5341034a-5c70-550f-94f0-6292fdc42b66" :answer/id #uuid "5341034a-5c70-550f-94f0-6292fdc42b66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a7772d20-a081-52a3-96c2-6ccd8c426e27" :answer/id #uuid "a7772d20-a081-52a3-96c2-6ccd8c426e27" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "100" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c6a11e57-9c69-5b62-be44-f709d7198d5a" :answer/id #uuid "c6a11e57-9c69-5b62-be44-f709d7198d5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{100}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110777 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8e575533-586b-5027-be32-c520f60008c9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8e575533-586b-5027-be32-c520f60008c9" :question/id #uuid "8e575533-586b-5027-be32-c520f60008c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-53034" :question/problem "![](images/cd/cd63e1c0cc60e53240ad8e064add8bd7c4d2abb1971de69a10b8f414b9c92fc8.png)\n\nWhich of the figures above is a square?" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the hierarchy diagram of quadrilaterals, where each shape below another is a specific type of the one above it.\n\n![](images/1d/1dbe4c3e8ea97c0ac077c37143802366c5817d86965ab1dbc5abf54cd01d27c3.png)\n\nRemember that a square is a quadrilateral where all angles are right and all sides are congruent.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each shape in turn.\n\n- The shape $P$ is a rhombus. Its four sides are congruent, however, it has no right angle. Therefore, it is not a square.\n\n- The shape $Q$ is a trapezoid. The sides are not all congruent, so it is not a square.\n\n- The shape $R$ is a kite. Since the sides are not all congruent, it is not a square.\n\n- The shape $S$ is an isosceles trapezoid. It has sides that are not congruent, therefore, it is not a square.\n\nTherefore, none of the shapes is a square." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6b40255b-02ed-5f18-a9b0-bc40a8de74f6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6b40255b-02ed-5f18-a9b0-bc40a8de74f6" :answer-field/id #uuid "6b40255b-02ed-5f18-a9b0-bc40a8de74f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2b4c0eac-fa86-5d0f-ad29-b94003d62802" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9e42fe38-c8a4-5465-9eb5-cccda24add7f" "answer-a5d573c3-b1be-58e8-aa91-45870582e400" "answer-420c0d71-22fb-505e-a0b4-2f90923da981" "answer-80c55bb3-f653-5ace-a8e5-59f8dbbafd16" "answer-2b4c0eac-fa86-5d0f-ad29-b94003d62802"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9e42fe38-c8a4-5465-9eb5-cccda24add7f" :answer/id #uuid "9e42fe38-c8a4-5465-9eb5-cccda24add7f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$P$ only" :