ass. Given that the correlation coefficient is $\\rho ≈0.45,$ which of the following scatter plots corresponds to this situation?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the linear correlation coefficient $\\rho $ satisfies the inequality\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\rho \\le 1,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\rho =1$ indicates a perfect positive correlation, and $\\rho =-1$ indicates a perfect negative correlation.\n\nTherefore, since $\\rho ≈0.45,$ there is a *weak positive* linear correlation in the data.\n\n- The *positive* linear correlation means that the data points should be scattered along a line with a *positive* slope.\n\n- Since the correlation is *weak*, most of the points should be scattered *far* from the trend line.\n\nTherefore, this situation corresponds to the following scatter plot.\n\n![](images/31/31aef47ad76d8cd4c7e967ccc7b8ca523eb3a20af440454bc7908bbe9441c918.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2f1ba1af-342f-5fed-bb12-14097b1af01f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2f1ba1af-342f-5fed-bb12-14097b1af01f" :answer-field/id #uuid "2f1ba1af-342f-5fed-bb12-14097b1af01f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9f1744c8-9253-57a1-9385-88741010bd5c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-be854c2e-00b5-5189-95d0-d391ce579514" "answer-8a10c856-18f3-5372-ad82-c037bac0b67c" "answer-26ccb841-9c61-58c1-b74a-7d6ba6da7857" "answer-1cc1444b-fd8c-5102-acf6-a80893a9655f" "answer-9f1744c8-9253-57a1-9385-88741010bd5c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-be854c2e-00b5-5189-95d0-d391ce579514" :answer/id #uuid "be854c2e-00b5-5189-95d0-d391ce579514" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/10/10408bda83013b4decbf51370d20018004a1086a538322abbd0b9da1b910e4f2.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a10c856-18f3-5372-ad82-c037bac0b67c" :answer/id #uuid "8a10c856-18f3-5372-ad82-c037bac0b67c" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/14/14258fd15361beae5d6e0655e81051b2e4bfd95d20b05dc98113558e43412f41.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-26ccb841-9c61-58c1-b74a-7d6ba6da7857" :answer/id #uuid "26ccb841-9c61-58c1-b74a-7d6ba6da7857" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/a8/a866fcee0e975c0741299a5e1504470dbae44e18b541149c7d5e1e2acb9b32bd.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1cc1444b-fd8c-5102-acf6-a80893a9655f" :answer/id #uuid "1cc1444b-fd8c-5102-acf6-a80893a9655f" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/ec/ec4b106cf763a4c54ee2b1d8eecf6e7b91e371b0dd38198502bd433ef7e6e371.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9f1744c8-9253-57a1-9385-88741010bd5c" :answer/id #uuid "9f1744c8-9253-57a1-9385-88741010bd5c" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/ec/ec7a1b76ebbcc4965824be26bc4b1e630167b032855498df6d492a61461fecf9.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083521 :question/problem "It is known that there is a linear correlation between the number of years passed since $2000$ and the population of a particular town. Given that the correlation coefficient is $\\rho ≈0.9,$ which of the following scatter plots corresponds to this situation?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the linear correlation coefficient $\\rho $ satisfies the inequality\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\rho \\le 1,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\rho =1$ indicates a perfect positive correlation, and $\\rho =-1$ indicates a perfect negative correlation.\n\nTherefore, since $\\rho ≈0.9,$ there is a *strong positive* linear correlation in the data.\n\n- The *positive* linear correlation means that the data points should be scattered along a line with a *positive* slope.\n\n- Since the correlation is *strong*, most of the points should lie *close* to the trend line.\n\nTherefore, this situation corresponds to the following scatter plot.\n\n![](images/aa/aac79b793bde599899ff7ff8ca880e198bd5481178c2c5a0e2ac96acf223bdaa.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186080021 :answer-field/correct 17592186080025 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186084452 :tutorial/content "There is a **linear correlation** between two sets of paired observations if the data points on the corresponding scatter plot are located along a straight line.\n\nWe say that the correlation is **positive** if the corresponding trend line has a *positive slope*. Similarly, we say that the correlation is **negative** if the corresponding trend line has a *negative slope*.\n\nWe have a **strong** correlation if the data points lie *close* to the corresponding trend line. Similarly, we have a **weak** correlation if the data points are scattered *far* from the corresponding trend line.\n\nLet's see a few examples:\n\n| ![](images/cd/cdd335fda9e91cbf7cdb05ad18065630985c50adb788df980708d822f7a5e8e9.png) | **Strong positive** linear correlation:\n\n- The trend line has a *positive* slope.\n\n- The data points lie *close* to the trend line. |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![](images/9b/9b288c25fb0993a714768e3e2e9caf23a11f2629950eb03b138acfc0aa6c17cf.png) | **Weak positive** linear correlation: \n\n- The trend line has a *positive* slope.\n\n- The data points lie *far* from the trend line. |\n| ![](images/36/3680700a5e4e4e196db6ffe106535ad784567b9fbed85e5005cbb6e49a476860.png) | **Strong negative** linear correlation:\n\n- The trend line has a *negative* slope.\n\n- The data points lie *close* to the trend line. |\n| ![](images/07/076440b257a78474e9f1b3129ec448a407bb1b49215a29251d8e929cadaeb984.png) | **Weak negative** linear correlation:\n\n- The trend line has a *negative* slope.\n\n- The data points lie *far* from the trend line. |\n| ![](images/ed/ed266d09a86d7200c02f004cd9bb3a87f75693462ff8846f7f3cc1ed4b66ed63.png) | **No linear correlation**:\n\n- The data points are scattered randomly. |" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186084490 :tutorial/content "The linear **correlation coefficient** $\\rho$ (the Greek letter rho, pronounced \"row\") is a real number between $-1$ and $1$ that shows the strength of a linear correlation. It has the following properties:\n\n- $\\rho = 1$ indicates a perfect positive correlation\n\n- $\\rho = -1$ indicates a perfect negative correlation\n\n- $\\rho = 0$ indicates no (linear) correlation\n\nThe approximate value of $\\rho$ can be determined from the scatter plot.\n\n| ![](images/09/09d585da995df4e5a67b022816eec246113171d3aad15dcb57d82c766dcb7d18.png) | For a strong positive correlation, we have $0.7 \\leq \\rho \\leq 1.$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![](images/9b/9b288c25fb0993a714768e3e2e9caf23a11f2629950eb03b138acfc0aa6c17cf.png) | For a weak positive correlation, we have $0.3 \\leq \\rho \\lt 0.7.$ |\n| ![](images/36/3680700a5e4e4e196db6ffe106535ad784567b9fbed85e5005cbb6e49a476860.png) | For a strong negative correlation, we have $-1 \\leq \\rho \\leq -0.7.$ |\n| ![](images/92/92b65a115fd1621303a248de8ae03d05392827914f5200f267d368867d511ae5.png) | For a weak negative correlation, we have $-0.7 \\lt \\rho \\leq -0.3.$ |\n| ![](images/2c/2cf1e2c3e79940229fc85c10d5bccdfed17afe0759cc897d53e5421328b21466.png) | For little or no correlation, we have $-0.3 < \\rho < 0.3.$ |" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083427 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129766 :question/worked-solution "Notice that our solid can be written as a type II region: \n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 6yz+12\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{6yz+12}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[x]_{x=0}^{x=6yz+12}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(6yz+12)-0\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}6yz+12\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[3y{z}^{2}+12z]_{z=0}^{z=1}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(3y(1)^{2}+12(1))-0\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}3y+12\\,dy \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}+12y]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}({2}^{2}-0)+12(2-0) \\\\  & =30.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186281297 :question/worked-solution "Notice that our solid can be written as a type III region: \n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,-1\\le z\\le 0,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 5-3{z}^{2}\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{5-3{z}^{2}}dy\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}[y]_{y=0}^{y=5-3{z}^{2}}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}5-3{z}^{2}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[5z-{z}^{3}]_{z=-1}^{z=0}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}0-(5(-1)-(-1)^{3})\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}5-1\\,dx \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{1}dx \\\\  & =4[x]_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =4(1-0) \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186235408 :question/worked-solution "First, we need to determine the projection of the intersection of our surfaces onto the $yz$-plane. So, let's find where they intersect.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2+{y}^{2}+4{z}^{2} & =-1+2{z}^{2} \\\\ {y}^{2}+2{z}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {y}^{2}+2{z}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the projection of the intersection in the $yz$-plane is an ellipse.\n\nNotice that our solid can be written as a type II region: \n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,-2+{y}^{2}+4{z}^{2}\\le x\\le -1+2{z}^{2}\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the interior of the ellipse ${y}^{2}+2{z}^{2}=1.$ \n\nAs a result, the volume of $R$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-2+{y}^{2}+4{z}^{2}}^{-1+2{z}^{2}}\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-1+2{z}^{2})-(-2+{y}^{2}+4{z}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}1-{y}^{2}-2{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the boundary of $D$ consists of \n\n- the lower part $z=-\\sqrt{\\frac{1-{y}^{2}}{2}},$ and\n\n- the upper part $z=\\sqrt{\\frac{1-{y}^{2}}{2}},$\n\nfor $-1\\le y\\le 1.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}1-{y}^{2}-2{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{(1-{y}^{2})/2}}^{\\sqrt{(1-{y}^{2})/2}}\\,1-{y}^{2}-2{z}^{2}\\,dz\\,dy.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f & ={(-\\sqrt{\\frac{1-{y}^{2}}{2}})}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{\\frac{1-{y}^{2}}{2}})}^{2}+(1-{y}^{2}-2{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{y}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{1-{y}^{2}}{2}+(1-{y}^{2}-2{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =2-2{y}^{2}-2{z}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186281316 :question/worked-solution "![](images/8e/8e5f3095cac4e068e54d9b3ac2bb55dc4789e7ca68d4524dce4d25a55abd5be6.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type III region\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 4-2x-4z\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the projection of $R$ onto the $xz$-plane.\n\nTo find the top boundary curve of $D$ in the form $z=z(x),$ we substitute $y=0$  into the equation $y=4-2x-4z:$\n\n$$\n0=4-2x-4z\\,⟹\\,z=1-\\frac{x}{2}\n$$\n\nThen, we have\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1-\\frac{x}{2}\\},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/76/76fcca4251a904a08ac2f6ba8181d92c2c2fa7e07e596ef6276f1d21b574817a.png)\n\nHence, the type III representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1-\\frac{x}{2},\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 4-2x-4z\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x/2}{\\int }_{0}^{4-2x-4z}dy\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x/2}[y]_{y=0}^{y=4-2x-4z}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x/2}(4-2x-4z)-0\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x/2}4-2x-4z\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[(4-2x)z-2{z}^{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=1-x/2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}((4-2x)(1-\\frac{x}{2})-2{(1-\\frac{x}{2})}^{2})-0\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(1-\\frac{x}{2})((4-2x)-2(1-\\frac{x}{2}))\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2}(2-x)(2-x)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2-2x+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={[2x-{x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =(2(2)-{2}^{2}+\\frac{{2}^{3}}{6})-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "activity-3acbe0bd-f475-593d-b042-bf6068b13815" :activity/id #uuid "3acbe0bd-f475-593d-b042-bf6068b13815" :activity/title "Calculating Volumes of Solids Using Triple Integrals" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048997 :activity/course 17592186046660 :activity/steps ["step-5f678a58-ebc6-50b7-bfbb-3b3bd2f77536" "step-c60f261b-2160-5d1d-a644-128afd94f52c" "step-2c68a282-fb8d-5473-b214-328eb1dfb504" "step-a29fc4a4-b0fb-5b9b-a936-4edfa87ff06b" "step-b8e034ac-74ed-5ee7-86d4-526d9fcddec2"] :activity/first-step "step-5f678a58-ebc6-50b7-bfbb-3b3bd2f77536" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-5f678a58-ebc6-50b7-bfbb-3b3bd2f77536" :step/id #uuid "5f678a58-ebc6-50b7-bfbb-3b3bd2f77536" :step/content 17592186129762 :step/next "step-c60f261b-2160-5d1d-a644-128afd94f52c" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c60f261b-2160-5d1d-a644-128afd94f52c" :step/id #uuid "c60f261b-2160-5d1d-a644-128afd94f52c" :step/content 17592186129766 :step/next "step-2c68a282-fb8d-5473-b214-328eb1dfb504" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-2c68a282-fb8d-5473-b214-328eb1dfb504" :step/id #uuid "2c68a282-fb8d-5473-b214-328eb1dfb504" :step/content 17592186281297 :step/next "step-a29fc4a4-b0fb-5b9b-a936-4edfa87ff06b" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-a29fc4a4-b0fb-5b9b-a936-4edfa87ff06b" :step/id #uuid "a29fc4a4-b0fb-5b9b-a936-4edfa87ff06b" :step/content 17592186235408 :step/next "step-b8e034ac-74ed-5ee7-86d4-526d9fcddec2" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-b8e034ac-74ed-5ee7-86d4-526d9fcddec2" :step/id #uuid "b8e034ac-74ed-5ee7-86d4-526d9fcddec2" :step/content 17592186281316 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186115357 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b02721d3-3788-51ae-8661-116da5ef0a5d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186115358 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6aa9a0d3-7eb3-556d-9424-29863addab07"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186115359 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-103a5626-5d09-5d8a-8f7a-23c1d1957e59" "question-e6ffaa7a-7878-5d6e-9066-50d06972d7db"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186115360 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-37c8a7b8-bbbe-57c2-8145-8ab238486f8f" "question-a27e56fa-3bc7-534d-a7f8-e4811aec35ea"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-b02721d3-3788-51ae-8661-116da5ef0a5d" :question/id #uuid "b02721d3-3788-51ae-8661-116da5ef0a5d" :question/math-academy-id "q-251067" :question/problem "![](images/45/45ab2798a4635050c736dadeeef49baa8ac46119c1ec797baa1c85116dd5c0d7.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to the nearest integer, the area of $△ABC$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of a right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nNotice that relative to the given angle $∠B,$ we have the length of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ and need to determine the length of the adjacent side $\\overset{―}{BC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $BC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B) & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({28}^{∘}) & =\\frac{7}{BC} \\\\ BC\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡({28}^{∘}) & =7 \\\\ BC & =\\frac{7}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡({28}^{∘})} \\\\ BC & =13.165…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 7\\cdot (13.165…) \\\\  & =46.077… \\\\  & ≈46,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-57db4a4b-39d1-5ddd-903e-239d50390fbf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-57db4a4b-39d1-5ddd-903e-239d50390fbf" :answer-field/id #uuid "57db4a4b-39d1-5ddd-903e-239d50390fbf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-ff2b1843-2999-5d65-92ea-422203627456" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ff2b1843-2999-5d65-92ea-422203627456"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ff2b1843-2999-5d65-92ea-422203627456" :answer/id #uuid "ff2b1843-2999-5d65-92ea-422203627456" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "46" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6aa9a0d3-7eb3-556d-9424-29863addab07" :question/id #uuid "6aa9a0d3-7eb3-556d-9424-29863addab07" :question/math-academy-id "q-76772" :question/problem "![](images/5f/5ff3d7cda0ee3fbc807a4bacbd3a739d72d83d0020271936ba77e6afbc89b83f.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A)=\\frac{5}{8},$ calculate the area (in square units) of $△ABC$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A)=\\frac{5}{8}.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AC} \\\\ \\frac{5}{8} & =\\frac{3x-2}{4x} \\\\ 5(4x) & =8(3x-2) \\\\ 20x & =24x-16 \\\\ -4x & =-16 \\\\ x & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =3x-2=3(4)-2=10, \\\\ AC & =4x=4(4)=16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 16\\cdot 10 \\\\  & =80.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bf6520db-ba96-51a1-ba7a-da9bb9952c12"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bf6520db-ba96-51a1-ba7a-da9bb9952c12" :answer-field/id #uuid "bf6520db-ba96-51a1-ba7a-da9bb9952c12" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f39c66b1-408a-5513-9867-cca6bf90979c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-10febb40-3e61-5498-b341-2e960bc67956" "answer-c3c85d34-5143-53b7-b849-f90f1422f396" "answer-03bbd126-6acb-5690-838d-8ee45699a1cd" "answer-f39c66b1-408a-5513-9867-cca6bf90979c" "answer-d2228e8f-34bb-59f8-8622-1b01b35e002d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-10febb40-3e61-5498-b341-2e960bc67956" :answer/id #uuid "10febb40-3e61-5498-b341-2e960bc67956" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "100" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c3c85d34-5143-53b7-b849-f90f1422f396" :answer/id #uuid "c3c85d34-5143-53b7-b849-f90f1422f396" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "140" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-03bbd126-6acb-5690-838d-8ee45699a1cd" :answer/id #uuid "03bbd126-6acb-5690-838d-8ee45699a1cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "70" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f39c66b1-408a-5513-9867-cca6bf90979c" :answer/id #uuid "f39c66b1-408a-5513-9867-cca6bf90979c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "80" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d2228e8f-34bb-59f8-8622-1b01b35e002d" :answer/id #uuid "d2228e8f-34bb-59f8-8622-1b01b35e002d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "90" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-103a5626-5d09-5d8a-8f7a-23c1d1957e59" :question/id #uuid "103a5626-5d09-5d8a-8f7a-23c1d1957e59" :question/math-academy-id "q-54311" :question/problem "![](images/93/93489f5dd12c8dbbde799b4047965a89e4204f151c0b4dfc36286392775a05e2.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{3}{4},$ calculate the area (in square units) of $△ABC$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{3}{4},$ where $\\theta =m∠C.$ Notice we're also given the length of the side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ adjacent to $∠C.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to find the length of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AB}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{AB}{AC} \\\\ \\frac{3}{4} & =\\frac{AB}{8} \\\\ AB & =\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot 8 \\\\ AB & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot AB \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 8\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-212da286-56fc-5fc9-a549-6eb30bfa1622"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-212da286-56fc-5fc9-a549-6eb30bfa1622" :answer-field/id #uuid "212da286-56fc-5fc9-a549-6eb30bfa1622" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-78722c9d-5692-5b7d-92d9-774b722e2b9f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-144f72ca-e0e9-5b1f-afad-c4334c647f5a" "answer-8e5a608a-2633-57f3-8bc5-95ba9b7b776f" "answer-bdb8b318-4d13-5788-8e10-66af9466935c" "answer-78722c9d-5692-5b7d-92d9-774b722e2b9f" "answer-97f63a0d-7159-5465-a875-d1797cd5193b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-144f72ca-e0e9-5b1f-afad-c4334c647f5a" :answer/id #uuid "144f72ca-e0e9-5b1f-afad-c4334c647f5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8e5a608a-2633-57f3-8bc5-95ba9b7b776f" :answer/id #uuid "8e5a608a-2633-57f3-8bc5-95ba9b7b776f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bdb8b318-4d13-5788-8e10-66af9466935c" :answer/id #uuid "bdb8b318-4d13-5788-8e10-66af9466935c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-78722c9d-5692-5b7d-92d9-774b722e2b9f" :answer/id #uuid "78722c9d-5692-5b7d-92d9-774b722e2b9f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-97f63a0d-7159-5465-a875-d1797cd5193b" :answer/id #uuid "97f63a0d-7159-5465-a875-d1797cd5193b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "32" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e6ffaa7a-7878-5d6e-9066-50d06972d7db" :question/id #uuid "e6ffaa7a-7878-5d6e-9066-50d06972d7db" :question/math-academy-id "q-54310" :question/problem "![](images/7d/7d996bfd2f4fa9822cae6284a3168f20911dbfd735a9b9c3c261fd30262b08e6.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{4}{5},$ calculate the area (in square units) of $△ABC$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AB\\cdot AC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{4}{5},$ where $\\theta =m∠B.$ Notice we're also given the length of the side $\\overset{―}{AB}$ adjacent to $∠B.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to find the length of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{AC}{AB} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & =\\frac{AC}{10} \\\\ AC & =\\frac{4}{5}\\cdot 10 \\\\ AC & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AB\\cdot AC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 10\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =40.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4f2f9f45-9c27-584a-80bf-964cb508c5a9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4f2f9f45-9c27-584a-80bf-964cb508c5a9" :answer-field/id #uuid "4f2f9f45-9c27-584a-80bf-964cb508c5a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-58b72fb6-94d0-5793-885f-37560956678b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-06e1b2ed-d909-5332-901e-47b5d044be00" "answer-83c14a6a-aa9b-5f1e-b230-960eda1989c4" "answer-58b72fb6-94d0-5793-885f-37560956678b" "answer-c8e0e20d-15a8-5b1e-857a-3401c73e5ef5" "answer-ee3e3e3e-4b48-556f-bd2d-7fb42ec66303"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-06e1b2ed-d909-5332-901e-47b5d044be00" :answer/id #uuid "06e1b2ed-d909-5332-901e-47b5d044be00" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-83c14a6a-aa9b-5f1e-b230-960eda1989c4" :answer/id #uuid "83c14a6a-aa9b-5f1e-b230-960eda1989c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "35" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-58b72fb6-94d0-5793-885f-37560956678b" :answer/id #uuid "58b72fb6-94d0-5793-885f-37560956678b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "40" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c8e0e20d-15a8-5b1e-857a-3401c73e5ef5" :answer/id #uuid "c8e0e20d-15a8-5b1e-857a-3401c73e5ef5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "45" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ee3e3e3e-4b48-556f-bd2d-7fb42ec66303" :answer/id #uuid "ee3e3e3e-4b48-556f-bd2d-7fb42ec66303" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "50" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-37c8a7b8-bbbe-57c2-8145-8ab238486f8f" :question/id #uuid "37c8a7b8-bbbe-57c2-8145-8ab238486f8f" :question/math-academy-id "q-124469" :question/problem "![](images/fb/fb14c05b065e8f3745dd6f1f3ad793abef565dac91047a89663c588519eabaaf.png)\n\nFind the area (in square units) of $△ABC$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AB.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $m∠A={30}^{∘}.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AB}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AB} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘}) & =\\frac{2x}{\\sqrt{3}\\,x+3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} & =\\frac{2x}{\\sqrt{3}\\,x+3} \\\\ \\sqrt{3}(\\sqrt{3}\\,x+3) & =3\\cdot 2x \\\\ 3x+3\\sqrt{3} & =6x \\\\ 3\\sqrt{3} & =3x \\\\ x & =\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =2x=2\\sqrt{3}, \\\\ AB & =\\sqrt{3}\\,x+3=\\sqrt{3}\\,(\\sqrt{3})+3=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot BC\\cdot AB \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a5a1cb85-7c02-5720-9e61-95e73cfc95bc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a5a1cb85-7c02-5720-9e61-95e73cfc95bc" :answer-field/id #uuid "a5a1cb85-7c02-5720-9e61-95e73cfc95bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a918ba21-6ada-5d09-a9a5-3eb5cd344e3e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-53039a13-f4a7-5f9b-b1d9-815fc1fb1dfe" "answer-d24d2498-db78-5a72-aa48-8c5a764dbe38" "answer-a9db3b66-a2aa-5bc6-9473-81fc00a121e7" "answer-a918ba21-6ada-5d09-a9a5-3eb5cd344e3e" "answer-77d9e7d2-0bd0-5206-b702-000e149b567e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-53039a13-f4a7-5f9b-b1d9-815fc1fb1dfe" :answer/id #uuid "53039a13-f4a7-5f9b-b1d9-815fc1fb1dfe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d24d2498-db78-5a72-aa48-8c5a764dbe38" :answer/id #uuid "d24d2498-db78-5a72-aa48-8c5a764dbe38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a9db3b66-a2aa-5bc6-9473-81fc00a121e7" :answer/id #uuid "a9db3b66-a2aa-5bc6-9473-81fc00a121e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a918ba21-6ada-5d09-a9a5-3eb5cd344e3e" :answer/id #uuid "a918ba21-6ada-5d09-a9a5-3eb5cd344e3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-77d9e7d2-0bd0-5206-b702-000e149b567e" :answer/id #uuid "77d9e7d2-0bd0-5206-b702-000e149b567e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a27e56fa-3bc7-534d-a7f8-e4811aec35ea" :question/id #uuid "a27e56fa-3bc7-534d-a7f8-e4811aec35ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-251195" :question/problem "![](images/24/243d382164750cdeb771f8630c3df642abcb034b3ddeb3c919f0b5f6b4fbff33.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to one decimal place, the area of $△ABC$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $m∠B={72}^{∘}.$ Notice that relative to $∠B,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{BC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B) & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({72}^{∘}) & =\\frac{3x+4}{2x-1} \\\\ (2x-1)\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡({72}^{∘}) & =3x+4 \\\\ 2x\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡({72}^{∘})-\\operatorname{tan}⁡({72}^{∘}) & =3x+4 \\\\ x(2\\operatorname{tan}⁡({72}^{∘})-3) & =4+\\operatorname{tan}⁡({72}^{∘}) \\\\ x & =\\frac{4+\\operatorname{tan}⁡({72}^{∘})}{2\\operatorname{tan}⁡({72}^{∘})-3} \\\\ x & =2.243\\,0…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =2x-1=2(2.243\\,0…)-1=3.486\\,1…, \\\\ AC & =3x+4=3(2.243\\,0…)+4=10.729\\,1….\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}(10.729\\,1…)(3.486\\,1…) \\\\  & =18.701\\,3… \\\\  & ≈18.7,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-465a3d16-9f8e-5bfe-9832-80996f5e185e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-465a3d16-9f8e-5bfe-9832-80996f5e185e" :answer-field/id #uuid "465a3d16-9f8e-5bfe-9832-80996f5e185e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-069c4b39-9d6f-58dc-9a57-eb50cdee63fa" :answer-field/choices ["answer-069c4b39-9d6f-58dc-9a57-eb50cdee63fa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-069c4b39-9d6f-58dc-9a57-eb50cdee63fa" :answer/id #uuid "069c4b39-9d6f-58dc-9a57-eb50cdee63fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18.7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186116453 :tutorial/content "Consider the right triangle $\\triangle ABC$ shown below.\n\n![](images/3f/3f7de9810f4acf33b504eb010d641e99811de82eed919e4340b5e68d414269ca.png)\n\nThe area of this right triangle is\n\n$$\n\\mathcal A = \\dfrac 1 2 ab.\n$$\n\nBut how can we calculate the area if we only know one side and one angle, as in the triangle below? \n\n![](images/c1/c1e5331333639f4d8e4f7b4cb3fee30ed1a7a889968844ae2b10961c5ae8e3ef.png)\n\nWe can follow the two steps below.\n\n**Step 1**: Calculate the missing side using the trigonometric ratios.\n\nHere, we need the adjacent side, and we know the opposite side. So, we should use tangent:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(B) & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡{30}^{∘} & =\\frac{3}{BC} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} & =\\frac{3}{BC} \\\\ BC\\sqrt{3} & =9 \\\\ BC & =\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ BC & =3\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Use the formula to calculate the area.\n\nNow that we know both sides of the triangle, we can just apply the formula as usual and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot 3\\sqrt{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186115434 :activity/expected-seconds 1020.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068727 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9a2ec726-00b7-5cc7-85a6-cb62e4711dd2" "question-48d8f1b2-776f-5613-8b52-d9e267acd25f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-9a2ec726-00b7-5cc7-85a6-cb62e4711dd2" :question/id #uuid "9a2ec726-00b7-5cc7-85a6-cb62e4711dd2" :question/math-academy-id "q-12796" :question/problem "Find $a$ if ${a}^{2}=40.$" :question/worked-solution "We take the square root of both sides of the equation and solve the resulting absolute value equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{a}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{40} \\\\ |a| & =\\sqrt{4\\cdot 10} \\\\ |a| & =\\sqrt{4}\\cdot \\sqrt{10} \\\\ |a| & =2\\sqrt{10} \\\\ a & =\\pm 2\\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-74304a95-1479-50c8-b9fd-11f3f0128771"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-74304a95-1479-50c8-b9fd-11f3f0128771" :answer-field/id #uuid "74304a95-1479-50c8-b9fd-11f3f0128771" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-000f3d81-c5d0-5946-b172-3bf3fe65444a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-34ac2f0d-2f64-5eae-b276-d1d7570929cb" "answer-9ba5b039-42c1-5f88-a8de-65c4f49d3c7a" "answer-000f3d81-c5d0-5946-b172-3bf3fe65444a" "answer-43f62726-6db5-59d8-a65d-6482ea48a157" "answer-492c1b78-ce03-55b1-9771-7be25a941eaf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-34ac2f0d-2f64-5eae-b276-d1d7570929cb" :answer/id #uuid "34ac2f0d-2f64-5eae-b276-d1d7570929cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=-2\\sqrt{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9ba5b039-42c1-5f88-a8de-65c4f49d3c7a" :answer/id #uuid "9ba5b039-42c1-5f88-a8de-65c4f49d3c7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=2\\sqrt{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-000f3d81-c5d0-5946-b172-3bf3fe65444a" :answer/id #uuid "000f3d81-c5d0-5946-b172-3bf3fe65444a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=\\pm 2\\sqrt{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-43f62726-6db5-59d8-a65d-6482ea48a157" :answer/id #uuid "43f62726-6db5-59d8-a65d-6482ea48a157" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=\\pm 2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-492c1b78-ce03-55b1-9771-7be25a941eaf" :answer/id #uuid "492c1b78-ce03-55b1-9771-7be25a941eaf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=\\pm 2\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-48d8f1b2-776f-5613-8b52-d9e267acd25f" :question/id #uuid "48d8f1b2-776f-5613-8b52-d9e267acd25f" :question/math-academy-id "q-56116" :question/problem "Find $a$ if ${a}^{2}-6=6.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the ${a}^{2}$ on one side of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{2}-6 & =6 \\\\ {a}^{2} & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the square root of both sides of the equation and solve the resulting absolute value equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{a}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{12} \\\\ |a| & =\\sqrt{12} \\\\ |a| & =\\sqrt{4\\cdot 3} \\\\ |a| & =\\sqrt{4}\\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\\\ |a| & =2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ a & =\\pm 2\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-825ca9e2-d349-54be-8ff8-677e119c487a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-825ca9e2-d349-54be-8ff8-677e119c487a" :answer-field/id #uuid "825ca9e2-d349-54be-8ff8-677e119c487a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-81d4dc11-5639-5bc7-9888-4db8339d8ad3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-81d4dc11-5639-5bc7-9888-4db8339d8ad3" "answer-174968af-4f97-5fc2-96c1-946a1318679f" "answer-1787098a-f4be-583e-8b74-371cf41e0f4e" "answer-1f6a6925-66ac-5529-a6b8-a5006b6b8998" "answer-260a6d7a-9e0e-525f-a529-7e99511654a1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81d4dc11-5639-5bc7-9888-4db8339d8ad3" :answer/id #uuid "81d4dc11-5639-5bc7-9888-4db8339d8ad3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm 2\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-174968af-4f97-5fc2-96c1-946a1318679f" :answer/id #uuid "174968af-4f97-5fc2-96c1-946a1318679f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm 2\\sqrt{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1787098a-f4be-583e-8b74-371cf41e0f4e" :answer/id #uuid "1787098a-f4be-583e-8b74-371cf41e0f4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm 3\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1f6a6925-66ac-5529-a6b8-a5006b6b8998" :answer/id #uuid "1f6a6925-66ac-5529-a6b8-a5006b6b8998" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm 4\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-260a6d7a-9e0e-525f-a529-7e99511654a1" :answer/id #uuid "260a6d7a-9e0e-525f-a529-7e99511654a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm \\sqrt{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068726 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-af7384d0-ffc3-51cc-833d-b329ee1b978c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-af7384d0-ffc3-51cc-833d-b329ee1b978c" :question/id #uuid "af7384d0-ffc3-51cc-833d-b329ee1b978c" :question/math-academy-id "q-111429" :question/problem "Solve for $z$ where $3{z}^{2}-\\frac{25}{12}=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the ${z}^{2}$ on one side of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{z}^{2}-\\frac{25}{12} & =0 \\\\ 3{z}^{2} & =\\frac{25}{12} \\\\ {z}^{2} & =\\frac{25}{36}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the square root of both sides of the equation and solve the resulting absolute value equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{z}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{25}{36}} \\\\ |z| & =\\frac{\\sqrt{25}}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\ |z| & =\\frac{5}{6} \\\\ z & =\\pm \\frac{5}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2138cdc1-7319-514a-94f4-c743a1b5525e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2138cdc1-7319-514a-94f4-c743a1b5525e" :answer-field/id #uuid "2138cdc1-7319-514a-94f4-c743a1b5525e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5d867956-1afa-545a-8d5e-158bee736d9a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-dae9e2a6-948b-5b95-a02c-61c1a8d0f2ce" "answer-363dd3dd-0402-51c3-b564-d0f77502fd2e" "answer-58910719-15f1-5c10-aba5-c08657d568a9" "answer-5d867956-1afa-545a-8d5e-158bee736d9a" "answer-9ee5e500-cf1f-5e17